'''thermo-battery''' (thėr″mō-bat′ėr-i), ''n.'' A thermopile.

'''thermocautery''' (thėr-mọ̄-kâ′tėr-i), ''n.'' [< Gr. θέρμη, heat, + E. ''cautery''.] A form of actual cautery in which the heat is produced by blowing benzin-vapor into heated spongy platinum on the inside of the cauterizing platinum-point.

'''thermochemical''' (thėr-mọ̄-kem′i-kạl), ''a.'' [< Gr. θέρμη, heat, + E. ''chemical''.] Of or pertaining to thermochemistry, or chemical phenomena as accompanied by the absorption or evolution of heat.

