'''thermo-electrometer''' (thėr″mō-ē-lek-trom′e-tėr), ''n.'' [< Gr. θέρμη, heat, + E. ''electrometer.''] An instrument for ascertaining the heating power of an electric current, or for determining the strength of a current by the heat it produces.

