'''thermo-element''' (thėr″mō-el′ẹ̄-ment), ''n.'' A thermo-electric couple. See ''thermo-electricity.''

'''thermo-excitory''' (thėr″mō-ek-sī′tọ̄-ri), ''a.'' [< Gr. θέρμη, heat, + E. ''excite'' + ''-ory.''] Causing the production of heat in the body.

